cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite this repository."
title: "Identifying Curatorial Voice: data and code"
abstract: >-
  Merged corpus, analysis code, and derived data for an article in preparation for
  the Journal of Digital History on cataloguing practice across the collections of
  the National Library of Scotland. Reduces catalogue records to a content-agnostic structural
  representation and clusters them blind to collection to recover shared cataloguing
  practice.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: James
    affiliation: University of Southampton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2682-6922"
version: "2.0.0-draft"
repository-code: "https://github.com/drjwbaker/nls-cataloguing-practice"
license: MIT              # code; data and derived data are CC0-1.0 (see LICENSE-DATA.md)
keywords:
  - cataloguing
  - catalogues as data
  - curatorial voice
  - cultural heritage
  - unsupervised clustering
  - reproducibility
